  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "One-two and overlap on half a pitch",
  "description": "An attacking pattern on half a pitch with ten outfield players and a keeper, no defenders. Centre-back A has the balls, and the players stand in position: central midfielder, striker, full-back and wide midfielder on both flanks.\n\nFirst through the middle: A passes to midfielder B, who turns, plays a one-two with striker C and shoots. C follows up for the rebound. Then down the flank: A passes to full-back D, who turns and passes to E. E drives inside to open the space down the line, D overlaps, gets the ball and crosses for C and B arriving in the box. Then do the same down the left.\n\nSwap B and C, and D and E, after a few rounds. Progression: add one or two defenders. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Turn to face forward as soon as you receive."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The wall plays the ball in front of the runner."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "The overlapping player calls and keeps their pace after the first touch."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Aim for the posts and look up before you shoot."
    }
  ],
